===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er}}

# [[cautious|Cautious]], [[suspicious]], [[wary]], [[hesitant]], or [[nervous]] about something; having [[reservations]] or [[concern]]s.
#: {{ux|en|Since he was bitten by a dog when he was young, he has always been '''leery''' of animals.}}
#* {{RQ:London Valley of the Moon|chapter=X|passage=“{{...}}He was one of their top gun-fighters—always up to his ears in the thick of any fightin' that was goin' on. He never was '''leery''' of anything on two feet, I'll say that much for'm.”}}
#* {{RQ:Lewis Main Street|chapter=XIV|passage=“He's so darn afraid you'll be offended if he smokes. You scare him. Every time he speaks of the weather you jump him because he ain't talking about poetry or Gertie—Goethe?—or some other highbrow junk. You've got him so '''leery''' he scarcely dares to come here.”}}
# {{lb|en|UK|obsolete|slang}} {{1|sly}}; [[artful]]; [[knowing]].
# {{lb|en|of a look or smile}} [[lecherous|Lecherous]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1902|title=The Fortunes of Oliver Horn|author=w:Francis Hopkinson Smith|url=https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/3417/pg3417.html|chapter=X|passage=And there was a particularly brutal villain with '''leery''' eyes, ugly mouth, with one tooth gone, and an iron jaw like a hull-dog's.}}

